    "description": "NixOS Package PRs for kmod, gnugrep, zstd-1.5.5, xz-5.4.3, bzip2-1.0.8, gzip packages on GitHub",
    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87350612?u=425a34036122961d0e04d7d68843c05f23639951&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This pull request updates <code class=\"notranslate\">kmod</code> from version 31 to 34.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The primary motivation is to resolve build failures encountered when building NixOS images (specifically <code class=\"notranslate\">makeModulesClosure</code>) with <strong>Linux Kernel 6.12+</strong>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Starting with Linux 6.12, the generated <code class=\"notranslate\">modules.builtin</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">modules.builtin.modinfo</code> files contain absolute paths from the build environment. The older version of <code class=\"notranslate\">depmod</code> (kmod v31) fails to handle these correctly within the Nix build sandbox, resulting in errors like:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"error: path '/nix/store/...-linux-6.12.68-modules-shrunk/lib' is not in the Nix store\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">error: path '/nix/store/...-linux-6.12.68-modules-shrunk/lib' is not in the Nix store\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updating to <code class=\"notranslate\">kmod</code> v34 fixes this issue as it correctly handles the new module path formats.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Changes</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Update Version</strong>: v31 -&gt; v34</li>\n<li><strong>Remove Patches</strong>:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Dropped <code class=\"notranslate\">module-dir.patch</code>. The upstream code has been refactored significantly (e.g., introduction of <code class=\"notranslate\">kmod_get_dirname</code>), making the old patch incompatible but functionality is preserved.</li>\n<li>Dropped <code class=\"notranslate\">musl.patch</code>: Included in upstream release.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Refreshed Patches</strong>:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Refreshed <code class=\"notranslate\">enable-static.patch</code> for v34 to continue supporting static builds.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Fix Symlinks</strong>: Removed manual creation of <code class=\"notranslate\">sbin</code> symlinks in <code class=\"notranslate\">postInstall</code> which were causing \"reflexive symlink\" errors during the fixup phase.</li>\n<li><strong>Build Configuration</strong>: Added <code class=\"notranslate\">--disable-manpages</code>. Version 34 requires <code class=\"notranslate\">scdoc</code> to build manual pages, which would introduce a new build dependency. Disabling them for now to keep the closure minimal and fix the build.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li>Built on platform:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-darwin</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Tested, as applicable:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> [NixOS tests] in [nixos/tests].</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> [Package tests] at <code class=\"notranslate\">passthru.tests</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tests in [lib/tests] or [pkgs/test] for functions and \"core\" functionality.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Ran <code class=\"notranslate\">nixpkgs-review</code> on this PR. See [nixpkgs-review usage].</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Tested basic functionality of all binary files, usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>.</li>\n<li>Nixpkgs Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Package update: when the change is major or breaking.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>NixOS Release Notes\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module addition: when adding a new NixOS module.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module update: when the change is significant.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> Fits [CONTRIBUTING.md], [pkgs/README.md], [maintainers/README.md] and other READMEs.</li>\n</ul>",
